+### Storage identity
+
+A Rust place keeps one address for its whole storage lifetime, whatever is stored into it, and a
+field at layout offset zero shares its container's address. In this model an aggregate place's
+**storage is the one JavaScript object that sits in it**, and every rule below exists so that
+object behaves like that storage. `examples/core-tests/120_aggregate_place_identity.rs` is the unit
+test, and `examples/known-gaps/audit_aggregate_place.rs` the regression it repairs.
+
