+  "fields are offsets" and "zero-offset aggregates share an anchor" do not hold for a heap element:
+  `&v[1].p` (offset zero) does not address-equal `&v[1]`, and `&v[1].z - &v[1]` is not
+  `offset_of!(Q, z)`. The identity of the element, and of each of its fields across stores, does
+  hold.
+- **A whole-enum store replaces payload objects.** A new enum value written over an enum place
